WEBVTT

00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:04.000
Aoi-san. I...

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:08.480
You gotta ask about it!

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:10.440
Y-You think?

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:11.240
Totally!

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:13.560
It's gotta be something important.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.990
He mighta been tryin' 
to tell you he likes you!

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.810
L-Likes me?

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:19.240
N-No way...

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.500
Holmes-san would never... 
Not someone like me.

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:24.200
Still, it don't cost nothin' to ask.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.000
I can't believe you spent a month <i>not</i> askin'.

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:32.000
The guy's so sharp, 
I have trouble bein' around him.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.010
But he's a good guy, so I'm behind ya, Aoi.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.620
Especially with Christmas comin' up!

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:41.150
Christmas, huh?

00:00:54.860 --> 00:01:00.450
<b>Holmes of Kyoto</b>

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:16.610
Episode 8

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:16.610
"Christmas Eve Tears and a Broken Alibi"

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.110
C'mon, I'm beggin' you!

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:20.610
You just gotta!

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:27.620
Aoi-san! You're here early.

00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:29.520
Y-Yeah...

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:32.450
Ueda-san, is something the matter?

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:34.730
You gotta back me up, Aoi-san.

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:37.130
I keep askin' Holmes, but he won't agree.

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:41.640
He wants the two of us to work 
part-time at a cafe he's opening.

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:44.400
Just the first week'll do.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.090
You're both handsome fellas.

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:47.550
You'd bring in customers like pandas!

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:50.140
Please don't compare me to a panda.

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:53.400
What kind of cafe is it?

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:56.260
One of those sweets cafes 
that're so trendy these days!

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:59.250
But the waiters're all attractive men,

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:01.160
so you could call it a hunk cafe!

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:03.490
A hunk cafe?

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:06.160
That's not a bad idea...

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:09.680
Where is this cafe?

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:12.670
As a matter of fact, it's on Kitayama Dori.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:14.670
Kitayama Dori?

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:17.670
<b>Kitayama</b>

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:17.670
That's close to my house. 
It's a really nice place.

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:22.200
Yes. It's in a very artistic area with 
botanical gardens and a concert hall.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:23.680
It's a wonderful place.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:31.920
Adult: 1,000 yen

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:26.320
I particularly like the botanical gardens.

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:29.120
Their annual passport is a mere 1,000 yen,

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:31.320
so I buy one every year.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:32.690
R-Really?

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:35.980
You're always sayin' you'd like to 
make this place a cafe someday.

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:37.190
I think it'd be good experience.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:40.180
Still... a week is a long time.

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:41.450
How about three days?

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:45.320
Let's make it four! 
Right up til Christmas Eve!

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:47.520
Very well. That's acceptable.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.840
Hell yeah! You got yerself a deal!

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:51.710
I'll be countin' on you both!

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.680
Both? Does he mean me, too?

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:57.310
It appears so.

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:59.710
Rikyu, bring tea for Aoi-san.

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:02.530
Fine.

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:04.320
Coming right up!

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:07.330
Um...

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:08.720
Is something the matter?

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:13.480
About what you were saying back at Genko-an...

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:20.130
That's right. How to put it...?

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:22.990
I wanted to thank you.

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:23.960
Thank me?

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:28.670
Yes. You've encouraged me so much. 
I owe you a great deal.

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:30.740
I wouldn't go that far...

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:34.710
If it would be all right with you, I'd like 
to take you out somewhere you'd enjoy.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:37.500
Well, I'm a little busy right now...

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:41.760
Do you mean... with that 
mixer you mentioned before?

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:46.250
Oh, I already turned them down.

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:48.260
I just wasn't into the idea.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:51.320
I see... But of course.

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:54.060
I just need to focus on my studies right now.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.020
Your studies?

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:59.770
My last round of test scores was pretty bad...

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:01.550
My mom said if I don't get them up,

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:04.780
I'll have to quit working here
 and go to cram school.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:07.830
I'm terribly sorry.

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:11.860
I didn't think a job here 
would end up affecting your grades.

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:13.380
This is a serious problem.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:16.040
Oh, it's just because 
I've been slacking. That's all.

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:17.280
Too bad.

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:19.040
I'll just take my old job back, then!

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:21.300
You can be quiet now, Rikyu.

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:26.300
Kiyo-nii, you're just too cool!

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:31.100
I've asked you to work on nights before tests,

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:33.230
so I feel I should take responsibility.

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:34.060
Responsibility?

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:37.220
Aoi-san, do your studying here from now on.

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:38.970
I'll watch over you.

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:40.690
<i>He's so close!</i>

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:45.940
As a token of thanks for all you do, 
I will improve your grades!

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:49.810
O-Okay. I'd appreciate that.

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:54.450
Ah, Holmes-kun's really here!

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:57.060
My, my! What brings you 
girls out all this way?

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:59.220
Seein' you, Holmes-kun.

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:02.960
Yeah, we're actually on our 
way to the Sanjo theater.

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:05.960
Sounds nice. I'd sure like 
to hit up a movie myself.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:08.280
You oughta come with us!

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:09.790
Can't on such short notice.

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:12.970
How about lettin' me know
 the next time you go?

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:15.720
Sure thing! It's a date!

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:19.290
Kiyo-nii's surrounded by girls, as usual.

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:20.570
Y-Yeah...

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:23.230
<b>Two Weeks Later</b>

00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:23.230
I don't believe it...

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:25.670
Your grades are up across the board!

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:28.200
Pays to have Holmes as a personal tutor, huh?

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:30.490
He was really helpful...

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:37.000
But when I told my mother that a Kyoto U
 student at my job was tutoring me...

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:39.960
she said we should have 
him over to thank him.

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:44.000
Score! You can introduce him to 
your folks and get their approval.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:45.900
I-It's not like that!

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:49.730
Apparently, all he really 
wanted was to thank me.

00:06:49.730 --> 00:06:52.120
So that's why he was helping me study.

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:55.140
Aw, that's all it was?

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:55.760
Yeah.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:58.770
I think I was under a misapprehension.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:00.180
A misapprehension?

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:03.020
Holmes-san is always kind and gentlemanly,

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:05.570
so I got it in my head that 
I was special to him...

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:07.530
But I think I had the wrong idea.

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:12.620
I've come to realize that's just 
how Holmes-san is with women.

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:17.410
I'm not special. I'm just a part-time coworker.

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:19.770
He even speaks formally around me.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:21.500
Feelin' heartbroken?

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:24.760
Oh, no, I wouldn't go far as that, exactly...

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:26.920
I-I just feel like...

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:28.920
I should keep my distance

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:34.020
and simply go back to admiring 
Holmes-san like I did before.

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:38.430
<i>But after I said that...</i>

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:41.440
<i>I ended up in this situation...</i>

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:44.020
It's quite a lovely room.

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:48.190
Um, please excuse my mother's 
aggressive politeness earlier!

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:53.500
The apple pie from Baikal and mame-mochi 
from Demachi Futaba were both delicious.

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:55.700
W-Well, that's good, at least...

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:59.700
And I'd always wanted to have a look 
at your grandfather's antiques.

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:02.460
But you came all this way,

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:06.460
and everything in the house
 turned out to be reproductions...

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:09.230
There wasn't anything of real value.

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:12.930
That just confirms how
 incredible you are, Aoi-san.

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:17.720
You singled out those
 Hakuin scrolls amidst all that.

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:19.720
You really do have a good eye.

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:22.450
R-Really, I just got lucky...

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:28.480
But being in a girl's room at home
 with family does take me back...

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:30.480
Take you back?

00:08:30.730 --> 00:08:34.840
Does it remind you of your old 
girlfriend... Izumi-san's room?

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:35.490
No.

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:38.460
I never actually saw Izumi's room,

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:41.750
though I did visit her house in Matsugasaki.

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:45.860
Matsugasaki? That's the luxury 
development near here, right?

00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:46.500
Yes.

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:48.280
Her parents were strict,

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:51.650
and they didn't like the idea of us 
being in her room alone together.

00:08:52.770 --> 00:08:57.010
Back then, I was so desperate to impress her.

00:08:57.430 --> 00:08:59.970
We oughta respect your parents' wishes.

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:01.520
We can have tea in the living room.

00:09:02.030 --> 00:09:04.510
It was so thoughtless of me.

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:06.940
Honestly, the thought of you 
desperate to impress someone...

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:11.630
Well, as a result of that, she dumped me hard.

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:14.590
Oh... But you're always so observant, Holmes-san.

00:09:14.590 --> 00:09:16.780
Why weren't you able to make up with her?

00:09:17.270 --> 00:09:21.000
Aoi-san, I may be on the observant side,

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:24.790
but when it comes to romance, 
I'm completely hopeless.

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:26.790
What do you mean?

00:09:26.990 --> 00:09:29.500
When my own feelings and 
expectations come into play,

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:33.290
I lose my ability to make 
objective judgments.

00:09:33.290 --> 00:09:34.300
I-I see...

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:36.650
I'm afraid that's what happened the other day.

00:09:36.650 --> 00:09:38.300
The other day?

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:42.430
You mean... you were interested 
in starting up a relationship?

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:44.310
I'm not sure.

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:47.980
Each time I try, I'm met with
 a reply I never expected

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:49.560
and it throws me off.

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:51.820
That's right, Aoi-san.

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:55.270
I'm interested in getting a look at that cafe.

00:09:55.270 --> 00:09:56.820
Would you like to accompany me?

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:06.920
Oh?

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:09.830
Someone's here wantin' to see Holmes.

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:12.090
Kiyotaka-kun...

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:14.840
<i>Izumi-san!</i>

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:16.270
I'm awful sorry.

00:10:16.270 --> 00:10:19.860
I saw her out front plumb lookin' 
like she was on the verge of tears.

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:23.850
I asked what was up, and she 
said she just had to talk to ya.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:29.200
It's been some time, hasn't it?

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:31.470
Y-Yes, it sure has...

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:33.360
U-Um...

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:36.090
Kiyotaka-kun, I was wonderin' if you 
could look into somethin' for me.

00:10:36.090 --> 00:10:38.360
Look into something? What, exactly?

00:10:40.590 --> 00:10:41.580
An alibi.

00:10:42.630 --> 00:10:43.780
I see.

00:10:44.280 --> 00:10:46.660
So you broke up with your last partner.

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:50.870
Your parents arranged a new match, 
and now you're marrying him.

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:53.000
Then, the other day

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:56.630
during your engagement party
 at your home in Matsugasaki,

00:10:57.150 --> 00:10:59.680
your fiancé left for an hour

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:02.140
at around 9 PM.

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:04.880
During that same time period,

00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:08.140
you saw a message posted by his 
old girlfriend in Momoyama saying,

00:11:08.840 --> 00:11:11.750
"He slipped out of his 
engagement party to see me,

00:11:11.750 --> 00:11:16.080
held me tight, and said I 
was the only one for him!"

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:23.230
She even came all the way to your 
workplace to tell you about it.

00:11:23.230 --> 00:11:24.410
Is that right?

00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:29.410
I asked him about it right away,

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:32.770
and he admitted that she was his ex.

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:36.420
But he said they broke up before we 
got set up and he wasn't cheatin'.

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:40.720
He said it ain't even possible 
to go from Matsugasaki to Momoyama

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:42.430
and back in an hour.

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:45.930
Yeah, that don't seem possible,
given the distance.

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:49.930
So, you want me to break his alibi?

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:51.150
That's right.

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:54.320
When we met, he seemed like 
an awful nice, faithful guy.

00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:55.940
I thought he was the one...

00:11:55.940 --> 00:12:00.200
<i>Her parents set them up, 
but she actually fell for him...</i>

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:07.700
I believe he did visit her 
on the day of the party.

00:12:08.670 --> 00:12:11.200
What'd he do? Take a helicopter?

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:12.230
No.

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:15.960
Also, I believe it's over between them.

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:17.430
Izumi-san.

00:12:17.430 --> 00:12:22.220
There are times in a relationship when 
it's necessary to look the other way.

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:25.720
Knowing that, are you 
prepared to learn the truth?

00:12:27.900 --> 00:12:31.800
My last cheatin' ex really 
put me through the ringer.

00:12:31.800 --> 00:12:34.060
I can't look the other way on this.

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:35.980
That's why I swallowed 
my pride an' came here!

00:12:36.370 --> 00:12:40.360
Very well. Then investigate the 
things I'm about to ask you for.

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:42.710
They'll be important evidence.

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:46.620
When you have everything ready,
 please contact me.

00:12:46.920 --> 00:12:47.690
Okay.

00:12:57.120 --> 00:12:58.880
<i>Christmas Eve, huh?</i>

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:01.650
<i>Holmes-san and Rikyu-kun are at the cafe,</i>

00:13:01.650 --> 00:13:04.260
<i>which is why I'm running the store...</i>

00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:10.390
Aoi-san, it's a bit early, 
but why don't you head out?

00:13:10.730 --> 00:13:11.960
Manager?

00:13:11.960 --> 00:13:15.340
You can check out the cafe where 
Kiyotaka and Rikyu are working.

00:13:15.340 --> 00:13:17.400
Th-Thank you.

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:19.280
Well, have fun.

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:19.650
Okay!

00:13:20.140 --> 00:13:24.430
I'm sure they'll be busy, so I'll just stop by.

00:13:27.210 --> 00:13:29.370
Huh?!

00:13:30.110 --> 00:13:31.910
D-Don't tell me...

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:34.160
This is the line?

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:38.520
Here you are.

00:13:39.870 --> 00:13:42.170
Hey, order already. You hear?

00:13:43.070 --> 00:13:44.920
So darn hot!

00:13:45.150 --> 00:13:49.150
The little one's kind of bossy, 
but that only makes him cuter!

00:13:49.960 --> 00:13:52.350
Today's their last day, right?

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:54.680
I'm gonna give 'em my contact info!

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:59.780
<i>I-It's like he's a totally different 
person from when he's at Kura.</i>

00:13:59.780 --> 00:14:03.310
<i>Well, looks like they don't need me here.</i>

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:06.780
Aoi-san!

00:14:08.520 --> 00:14:09.590
Holmes-san!

00:14:09.590 --> 00:14:12.200
I'm so glad I saw you.

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:16.720
Would you mind coming back after we close?

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:18.710
Wh-Why?

00:14:19.320 --> 00:14:21.640
I heard from Izumi.

00:14:21.640 --> 00:14:24.210
She's going to come by later with her fiancé.

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:32.010
<b>Kitayama</b>

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:35.220
I'm Yagashira Kiyotaka.

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:37.230
Tachibana.

00:14:39.930 --> 00:14:41.760
I've heard about you.

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:45.480
They call you the Holmes of Kyoto 
because you're rather astute.

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:50.490
No, I'm only called Holmes 
because my family name is Yagashira.

00:14:51.860 --> 00:14:54.220
This is about the engagement party, isn't it?

00:14:54.220 --> 00:14:57.130
It is. She didn't accept your excuse,

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:59.250
so she asked for my advice.

00:14:59.530 --> 00:15:00.800
Oh?

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:03.190
And when your beautiful 
classmate asked for help,

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:05.500
I'm sure you couldn't refuse.

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:09.190
Not so. I have a fiancée of my own, you see.

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:16.640
<i>I-I see... He wants Tachibana-san 
to let his guard down...</i>

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:19.170
Oh, is that so?

00:15:19.170 --> 00:15:20.160
Yes.

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:23.650
So my concern for Izumi-san is unbiased.

00:15:23.850 --> 00:15:26.520
I think you'll find
 you're concerned for nothing.

00:15:26.520 --> 00:15:28.120
I told Izumi the same.

00:15:28.600 --> 00:15:33.410
I couldn't possibly get from 
Matsugasaki to Momoyama in an hour.

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:37.940
Indeed, it's not possible 
by bus, subway, car, or motorcycle.

00:15:37.940 --> 00:15:41.410
Yet you still went to see her and returned.

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:45.670
Will you hear my theory?

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:49.220
First, why would you need to go

00:15:49.220 --> 00:15:53.490
to your ex-girlfriend's house during 
your engagement party, of all times?

00:15:53.490 --> 00:15:57.000
Was it because she, drunk and reckless,

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:59.920
sent you a threatening message?

00:15:57.560 --> 00:16:00.430
<b>I can't accept you dumping me like this.
Maybe I'll barge into your fiancée's place!</b>

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:04.530
If her house was really in Momoyama, 
you could have ignored it.

00:16:04.530 --> 00:16:07.850
But I suspect that she actually 
lives close to Kitayama Dori,

00:16:07.850 --> 00:16:10.070
and that she knows where Izumi-san lives.

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:16.200
In other words, she could have 
made a scene if she so desired.

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:18.960
You're a smart man, so you 
sneaked out through the garden.

00:16:18.960 --> 00:16:21.180
Then you stopped at a 
nearby convenience store

00:16:21.180 --> 00:16:22.960
and went to visit your ex.

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:26.830
When she started crying tears of joy, 
you held her tightly and apologized.

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:29.820
Perhaps you told her the marriage was your 
parents' decision and you had no choice.

00:16:30.540 --> 00:16:34.950
Then you offered her a settlement with the 
money you withdrew at the convenience store,

00:16:34.950 --> 00:16:37.460
and convinced her to stay away from you.

00:16:37.460 --> 00:16:41.330
In other words, your alibi was pure sophistry.

00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:43.940
It's true you never made 
a round trip to Momoyama.

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:46.900
But you did go see your ex-girlfriend
 who lived in the neighborhood.

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:50.980
At least, that's my theory.

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:54.990
Well, you're very imaginative. 
I'll give you that.

00:16:55.400 --> 00:16:59.490
Dismissing it as a flight of fancy
 seems a bit hasty.

00:17:00.090 --> 00:17:02.500
But that's all it is.

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:07.500
<i>From there, Holmes-san and Tachibana-san 
began a fierce exchange.</i>

00:17:08.030 --> 00:17:13.510
<i>Izumi-san offered testimony that Tachibana had
 withdrawn money from the convenience store.</i>

00:17:13.890 --> 00:17:16.080
<i>It seemed the sight of a man
 in a suit and sandals</i>

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:18.260
<i>was rather memorable
 for the employees there.</i>

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:22.560
<i>She also presented irrefutable
 evidence that his ex-girlfriend</i>

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:24.520
<i>did indeed live near Kitayama Dori.</i>

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:29.020
So what?

00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:32.030
Even if your theory is true,

00:17:32.350 --> 00:17:34.030
that means it's all over with her!

00:17:36.760 --> 00:17:39.280
You think Izumi-san can just accept that?!

00:17:39.480 --> 00:17:43.790
You're acting in bad faith, 
both with her and your ex-girlfriend!

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:47.540
Even I can tell that you're lying!

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:51.290
Even if you love someone, 
if you keep lying to them,

00:17:51.290 --> 00:17:53.440
they'll never be able to trust you!

00:17:53.440 --> 00:17:56.300
And that doesn't make a marriage!

00:17:56.560 --> 00:18:00.530
Even if it's awkward... 
Even if you get hurt...

00:18:00.530 --> 00:18:03.560
If you truly care about Izumi-san...

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:08.060
tell her the truth.

00:18:08.590 --> 00:18:10.110
Aoi-san...

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:13.320
S-Sorry, I know this doesn't concern me.

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:17.070
Thanks for sayin' it for me.

00:18:17.540 --> 00:18:22.080
I just... can't believe you'd lie like that...

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:28.200
I'm very sorry.

00:18:29.010 --> 00:18:31.360
Yagashira-san was right about everything.

00:18:32.440 --> 00:18:36.590
My ex-girlfriend and I were on the 
rocks when your parents' offer came up.

00:18:37.140 --> 00:18:38.950
I decided we were probably through,

00:18:38.950 --> 00:18:41.340
so I used that as a reason to break up.

00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:45.600
Then I met you for the first time, and...

00:18:46.230 --> 00:18:47.600
I'm embarrassed to say it, but...

00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:49.480
I fell in love at first sight.

00:18:51.010 --> 00:18:55.200
When I heard why you broke it off 
with your former fiancé,

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:57.840
I was afraid that if I brought 
up my old relationship,

00:18:57.840 --> 00:18:59.860
you'd leave me right away.

00:19:00.380 --> 00:19:02.730
That's why I lied about it.

00:19:03.290 --> 00:19:06.610
I didn't want to lose you.

00:19:07.140 --> 00:19:10.120
I am truly sorry.

00:19:11.270 --> 00:19:12.630
Tachibana-san...

00:19:12.820 --> 00:19:15.190
P-Please don't...

00:19:15.190 --> 00:19:17.120
Um...

00:19:17.120 --> 00:19:20.880
Aoi-san, I think it's time 
for us to take our leave.

00:19:21.080 --> 00:19:21.860
Yeah.

00:19:24.030 --> 00:19:26.390
I'm sorry about earlier.

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:29.000
I shouldn't have forced 
you to pretend to be my fiancée.

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:33.400
No, it's fine. It did seem to allay 
Tachibana-san's suspicions.

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:39.150
With the way you stared at me, 
I was worried I'd upset you.

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:40.960
I-I was a little surprised.

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:43.130
I didn't think I was staring...

00:19:43.690 --> 00:19:48.410
H-Holmes-san, don't you feel... 
a little weird about this?

00:19:49.180 --> 00:19:51.410
No. She and I really are over.

00:19:51.800 --> 00:19:53.480
I'm glad to hear it.

00:19:53.480 --> 00:19:56.160
Your speech back there was incredible.

00:19:56.160 --> 00:19:57.420
Oh, h-hardly!

00:19:57.600 --> 00:20:01.840
I just really understood how she felt,

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:03.930
and I couldn't keep it in.

00:20:04.150 --> 00:20:05.380
I see.

00:20:05.380 --> 00:20:09.520
You truly are a sensitive, 
straightforward person, aren't you?

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:11.490
Y-You think?

00:20:12.320 --> 00:20:15.560
That reminds me... 
It's Christmas Eve, isn't it?

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:16.690
It's really beautiful.

00:20:17.420 --> 00:20:18.070
Indeed.

00:20:19.640 --> 00:20:21.690
It's only a small token, but here.

00:20:21.980 --> 00:20:23.950
A Christmas present for you.

00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:26.640
Please open it.

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:28.950
Thank you!

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:31.200
Adult: 1,000 yen

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:33.460
U-Um...

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:36.370
It's the annual passport I mentioned before.

00:20:36.370 --> 00:20:39.460
Now you can enjoy 
the botanical gardens all year long.

00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:42.600
It's a wonderful place to go when 
you need to think or lift your spirits.

00:20:44.270 --> 00:20:45.440
What's the matter?

00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:48.510
Nothing. It's just so Holmes-like.

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:49.220
Oh, right!

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:52.730
This is also just a token, but...

00:20:53.040 --> 00:20:54.030
What's this?

00:20:54.030 --> 00:20:56.730
I like baking cookies,

00:20:56.940 --> 00:20:58.950
so I was hoping you'd accept these

00:20:58.950 --> 00:21:01.480
as a thank you for all you do.

00:21:04.150 --> 00:21:06.240
Oh heck...

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:10.740
Yeah, it's really cold.

00:21:13.680 --> 00:21:15.590
Your hands are red.

00:21:15.590 --> 00:21:17.750
You didn't bring gloves?

00:21:17.750 --> 00:21:19.260
N-No...

00:21:19.260 --> 00:21:22.260
You poor thing. They're like ice.

00:21:23.980 --> 00:21:26.380
U-Um, Holmes-san...

00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:28.640
Aoi-san...

00:21:28.980 --> 00:21:30.890
Y-Yes?

00:21:31.120 --> 00:21:33.770
Kiyo-nii, Aoi-san... Let's bail.

00:21:34.250 --> 00:21:36.020
R-Rikyu-kun?

00:21:36.020 --> 00:21:38.400
I finally got everything cleaned up.

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:42.500
Kiyo-nii didn't help out at all, 
so it was a ton of work.

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:45.530
Rikyu, you are really somethin' else.

00:21:46.730 --> 00:21:48.030
Let's go home.

00:21:48.290 --> 00:21:50.530
Y-Yeah, good idea.

00:21:52.860 --> 00:21:54.540
<i>That night on Christmas Eve...</i>

00:21:54.970 --> 00:21:57.540
<i>I wonder what Holmes-san was going to say.</i>

00:21:58.220 --> 00:22:00.540
<i>I couldn't find it in me to ask</i>

00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:05.240
<i>because I'd decided I'd draw a line.</i>

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:14.290
<b>Holmes of Kyoto</b>

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:51.880
"The Sound of the Bell at Gion"

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:57.060
Next Episode

00:23:37.210 --> 00:23:39.260
Another year over, I guess.

00:23:39.260 --> 00:23:41.920
We'll be having a party at my 
house for New Year's Eve.

00:23:41.920 --> 00:23:44.380
Really? Another party?

00:23:45.030 --> 00:23:48.490
Next time: "The Sound of the Bell at Gion."

00:23:48.490 --> 00:23:50.800
Holmes-san, you really are nasty.
